From 4513024e313312e7265d9984b9103bba0f214f3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:55:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/43] powerstatus: let the user choose a charge limit

Add a "Charge limit" submenu to the PowerStatus menu with "Full",
80 % and 60 %. Charging starts again 5 points below the limit. The
choice applies to every battery whose driver supports thresholds, and
the current one is ticked when all batteries share it. The submenu
only appears when at least one battery supports it, today on
ThinkPads.

The choices and the tick are pure logic with host tests.

Signed-off-by: Michael Spanier <spanier.michael@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit b6eb099bbd076c429753845827f93fa3c770ad1d)
